{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq75a81a","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"[ingest] Self-signed certs cannot shortcut local HTTPS; mkcert is required","summary":"TLS validates the cert’s issuer against the system trust store regardless of localhost, so a self-signed cert (its own untrusted issuer) is rejected. mkcert -install adds a trusted local CA (the password step), which is the only reason it works. HTTPS is needed ONLY for the inline-chat connector or off-localhost exposure; normal local use skips it.","created_by":"ingest","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq75a81a","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"[ingest] Self-signed certs cannot shortcut local HTTPS; mkcert is required","summary":"TLS validates the cert’s issuer against the system trust store regardless of localhost, so a self-signed cert (its own untrusted issuer) is rejected. mkcert -install adds a trusted local CA (the password step), which is the only reason it works. HTTPS is needed ONLY for the inline-chat connector or off-localhost exposure; normal local use skips it.","created_by":"ingest","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:08:57.822Z"}
